@startuml
!include style.iuml
' Sources: ClientPrograms.cpp; Server.cpp; ServerPrograms.cpp;
' Controller.cpp; ControllerAdmission.cpp; Executor.cpp.
title Finite motion · execution, controlled stop and lease loss
caption Starts with a prepared, running Executor program. Raw motor stops and homing use a different path.
footer Configured timing is shown, not a measured worst-case guarantee. Source-level behavior still needs full hardware qualification.
autonumber
box "M7 · UI" #EDF4FE
participant "Client\napplication worker" as C
end box
boundary "Serialized ICC\nurgent / normal lanes" as W #FFF5DF
box "M4 · IO" #EAF7F4
participant "Server\nIO dispatcher" as S
participant "Controller\nexecution worker" as O
participant "Executor" as E
participant "STEP HAL\nTIM2 / DMA" as H
end box

== Two different renewals ==
loop UI owner keepalive · every 50 ms while active
  C -> W : urgent io/trajectory/control: Renew{job IDs}
  W -> S : urgent service ready
  S -> O : control(Renew) under Controller mutex
  O -> O : renew valid owner deadlines to now + 250 ms
  O --> S : acknowledgement
  S --> W : urgent reply
  W --> C : record acknowledgement / error
end
note over C,O
  One renewal request in flight; late renewals do not revive expired jobs.
  Ownership renewal is separate from M4 pulse-schedule maintenance.
end note
loop M4 execution worker · notifications + up to 1 ms timed wait when active
  O -> H : preparePending(): fill requested DMA buffers
  O -> O : check faults, ownership lease and motion timeout
  O -> E : renew(id); service()
  opt Maintenance due · nominally every 40 ms
    E -> E : build next immutable schedule bank\ninclude stopping continuation from its boundary
    E -> H : splice(replacement, current boundary)
    H --> E : accepted, retry or error
    E -> E : advance committed frontier toward now + 80 ms
  end
  H -> H : hardware-timed STEP edges
  H -->> O : refill / completion notifications
end
note over E,H #EAF7F4
  The installed schedule already contains its brake.
  Continuing motion replaces future data before that boundary.
  Stopping does not need a new M7 plan.
end note

== Controlled stop · two ways to select the installed brake ==
alt Explicit axis/robot stop or action cancellation
  C -> W : urgent Stop{job or axis mask}\n(cancel also requests action cancellation)
  W -> S : control request / cancel notification
  S -> O : control(Stop); expand target to whole owned group
  O -> E : stop(id)
  E -> E : state = Braking; cease nominal schedule extension
  O --> S : stop request processed
  S --> W : acknowledgement
  W --> C : request acknowledged, NOT yet terminal
else UI renewal stops / link is lost
  ... no valid owner renewal arrives ...
  O -> O : owner deadline expires\n(or connectionLost() invalidates admission)
  O -> E : stop(id)
  E -> E : use already installed stopping continuation
  note over C,O #FFF5DF
    No reply from M7 is needed for this local selection.
    A disconnected UI cannot infer a confirmed physical stop.
  end note
end

== Completion and ownership release ==
H -> H : finish committed prefix, brake, then last STEP
H -->> O : completion notification
O -> E : service() observes all participating outputs complete
E --> O : Stopped + counts / error status
O -> S : bounded completion callback: copy result + notify
S -> S : dispatchPrograms(): observe completion record
S -> W : terminal action result: cancelled(Stopped)
S -> O : releaseJob(job) after completion cleanup
W --> C : ready notification; Client.run() dispatches result
C -> C : retain history; release pending action handle
note over C,H
  Natural completion follows the same result path with Completed.
  Communication failure can leave the UI result Unknown.
  Local faults / explicit Abort bypass braking and may invalidate references.
  Hardware-guard cessation is not a controlled-stop guarantee.
end note
@enduml
